It's the chart reference, in the form repo_name/chart_name. Both halves happen to have the same name.

First aws-ebs-csi-driver is the name of the Helm repository you added on your machine, using a command like:
bash
helm repo add aws-ebs-csi-driver https://kubernetes-sigs.github.io/aws-ebs-csi-driver

The name after repo add is just a local alias. You could have called it ebs or anything else, and then you'd write ebs/aws-ebs-csi-driver.

Second aws-ebs-csi-driver is the name of the chart inside that repository. This one is fixed by whoever published the chart.

This is the same idea as the error you hit earlier ("should be in form of repo_name/path_to_chart"). Instead of . (a chart in your local directory), you're pointing Helm at a chart in a remote repo.

The other parts of the command:

ebs-csi-driver is the release name (what you'd see in helm list). It's your choice and doesn't need to match the chart name.
--namespace kube-system installs it into that namespace.
--version 2.62.0 pins the chart version. This is not the same as the driver's app version.

